// C=αop(A)op(B)ᴴ+βC, where α and β are scalars, C is a Hermitian matrix stored in lower or upper mode, and A and B are matrices with dimensions op(A)n×k and op(B)n×k , respectively. Also, for matrix A and B
// op(A) and op(B)={A and Bif trans == CUBLAS_OP_NAᴴ and Bᴴif trans == [OpC]
// This routine can be used when the matrix B is in such way that the result is guaranteed to be hermitian. An usual example is when the matrix B is a scaled form of the matrix A: this is equivalent to B being the product of the matrix A and a diagonal matrix. For an efficient computation of the product of a regular matrix with a diagonal matrix, refer to the routine cublasdgmm().
// For references please refer to NETLIB documentation:
// cherk(), zherk() and
// cher2k(), zher2k()
//
// [Handle.Cherkx64] takes 64-bit sizes.
//
//   - handle: Handle to the cuBLAS library context
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix C lower or upper part is stored, the other Hermitian part is not referenced
//   - trans: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - n: Number of rows of matrix op( A), op( B) and C
//   - k: Number of columns of matrix op( A) and op( B)
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - a: < type > array of dimension lda x k with lda >= max(1, n) if transa == [OpN] and lda x n with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - b: < type > array of dimension ldb x k with ldb >= max(1, n) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x n with ldb >= max(1,k) otherwise
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - beta: Real scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0 then C does not have to be a valid input
//   - c: < type > array of dimension ldc x n, with ldc >= max(1, n). The imaginary parts of the diagonal elements are assumed and set to zero
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix C
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrExecutionFailed]: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: If n < 0 or k < 0, or if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or if lda < max(1, n) when trans == [OpN], and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or if ldc < max(1, n), or if alpha or beta are NULL, or if C is NULL when beta is not zero
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized
//
// Wraps cublasCherkx.
func cherkx(handle Handle, uplo FillMode, trans Operation, n int32, k int32, alpha *Complex64, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int32, b driver.DevicePtr, ldb int32, beta *float32, c driver.DevicePtr, ldc int32) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cublasCherkx"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fncherkx(handle, uplo, trans, n, k, alpha, uintptr(a), lda, uintptr(b), ldb, beta, uintptr(c), ldc), "cublasCherkx")
}

